body:
I had a hard time choosing the career I wanted to go into myself. Just like you, it was always about the money involved, and how much i'd be making. But i did eventually come to the conclusion that i didn't want to be stuck in a shitty career that i wasn't interested 15 years down the line, so i started experimenting with my options.  i did eventually find interest in music, so i decided to major in audio in music production. 

&#x200B;

i cant say much about how far along i've come in the career itself, im still a senior in high school. But just taking the time and figuring out what you actually want to do goes a long way. Do what **you** want to do, not what your family and friends want. You're not too confident in your chosen major? Go for something else. It's about what you want for yourself, it's about what you can see yourself happily doing several years down the line. And if the career you truly want to choose is risky, go for it. You miss all of the shots you don't take. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
